<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1937</h1><p class="ref-lede">1937 in world history: 37 events, 13 births, 28 deaths, 3 works, 5 states founded and 9 that came to an end. 719 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1933">1933</a><a href="/years/1934">1934</a><a href="/years/1935">1935</a><a href="/years/1936">1936</a><a href="/years/1937" aria-current="page">1937</a><a href="/years/1938">1938</a><a href="/years/1939">1939</a><a href="/years/1940">1940</a><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-19">19 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Howard Hughes sets a transcontinental air speed record</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hughes flew his H-1 racer from Burbank, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, to Newark, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, in 7 hours, 28 minutes and 25 seconds. The record stood for seven years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-16">16 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Wallace Carothers's nylon is patented</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">DuPont received the patent for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nylon">nylon</a>, invented by a team led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallace-carothers">Wallace Carothers</a>. The first fully synthetic fibre, it was used for stockings and then wartime <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parachute">parachutes</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-26">26 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">German and Italian aircraft bomb Guernica</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/condor-legion">Condor Legion</a>, with Italian support, bombed the Basque town on market day, killing hundreds of civilians. The attack inspired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso">Picasso</a>'s painting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guernica">Guernica</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/nazi-germany">Nazi Germany</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-3">3 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Margaret Mitchell wins the Pulitzer for Gone with the Wind</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Margaret Mitchell's novel of the Civil War and Reconstruction won the Pulitzer Prize for Fiction. A huge bestseller, it was filmed in 1939, though its portrayal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> is now widely criticised.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-6">6 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hindenburg airship bursts into flames at Lakehurst</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/airship">airship</a> Hindenburg caught fire while mooring in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, killing 36 people. Newsreel film and radio coverage of the disaster ended public faith in passenger airships.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-27">27 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Golden Gate Bridge opens to pedestrians</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 200,000 people walked across the new bridge on its opening day before cars were allowed the next. Its main span was then the longest of any suspension bridge.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-2">2 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Amelia Earhart disappears over the Pacific</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Amelia Earhart and navigator Fred Noonan vanished while searching for tiny Howland Island on the last long legs of their round-the-world flight. Despite a vast search, their fate has never been conclusively established.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-7">7 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Marco Polo Bridge Incident sparks war between China and Japan</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A night-time clash between Japanese and Chinese troops at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugou-bridge">Marco Polo Bridge</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> escalated into full-scale war. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-sino-japanese-war">Second Sino-Japanese War</a> merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and cost millions of Chinese lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo">Marco Polo</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yangtze-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-12">12 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japanese aircraft bomb and sink the US gunboat Panay</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese aircraft attacked the U.S. Navy gunboat Panay and three Standard Oil tankers on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, sinking the Panay, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> were not at war. It served on the Yangtze Patrol, begun after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-opium-war">Second Opium War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-13">13 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japanese troops capture Nanjing</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, and began weeks of mass killing, rape and looting. Estimates of the dead range from tens of thousands to over 300,000, and the massacre remains bitterly contested.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/greater-hamburg-act">Greater Hamburg Act</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Greater Hamburg Act was a Nazi German law of 1937 that redrew the boundaries of several northern German states.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-shanghai" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-shanghai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-shanghai">Battle of Shanghai</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Shanghai was fought from August to November 1937 in and around Shanghai, the first major battle of the Second Sino-Japanese War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona-may-days" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barcelona-may-days.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Crisis</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/barcelona-may-days">Barcelona May Days</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Barcelona May Days were street fighting in Barcelona from 3 to 8 May 1937 between anarchists and the POUM on one side and Republican and Communist forces on the other.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/cohen-plan">Cohen Plan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Cohen Plan was a forged document, presented as a communist plan to seize power in Brazil, that the government of Getúlio Vargas made public in September 1937.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/parsley-massacre">Parsley Massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Parsley Massacre was the killing of thousands of Haitians and Dominicans of Haitian descent in the Dominican borderlands in October 1937, on the orders of the dictator Rafael Trujillo.</p></div></li></ol></section>
