<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-china"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20China.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of China</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">War with Japan begins after the Marco Polo Bridge Incident</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-haiti"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Haiti.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Haiti</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Dominican dictator Rafael Trujillo's army bludgeons and bayonets 20,000–30,000 Haitians on the border in the Parsley Massacre.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/manchukuo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Manchukuo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Manchukuo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Manchukuo serves as the base for Japan's invasion of the rest of China after the Marco Polo Bridge incident; 'thought crime' is introduced and an emergency law mobilises society for total war.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/modernism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Modernism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Modernism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Nazis mount the Degenerate Art exhibition in Munich, and Picasso paints Guernica</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/zionism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Zionism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Zionism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">During the Arab Revolt of 1936–1939, the Peel Commission proposes partition and a transfer of Palestinian Arabs</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/kemalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kemalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kemalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The six principles are written into the constitution as state ideology</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/francoist-spain"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Francoist%20Spain.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Francoist Spain</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In April Franco merges the Falange Española de las JONS with the Carlist Comunión Tradicionalista to form the Falange Española Tradicionalista y de las JONS</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Two Japanese naval personnel and a Chinese guard are found dead at Hongqiao Airport, and the Japanese begin sending reinforcements to Shanghai</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Fighting begins between Chinese and Japanese forces in Zhabei, Wusong and Jiangwan, and on 14 August China declares its resistance to Japanese aggression</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The 36th Division's attack towards the Huangpu docks pushes the Japanese back but cannot break through</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Japanese 3rd and 11th Divisions land on the northeast coast, lengthening the front</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Baoshan falls on 6 September, and the Chinese hold Luodian for weeks at heavy cost</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The fight for Wusong Creek and Dachang ends with Dachang's fall on 26 October, and the Chinese withdraw from the city's urban centre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Japanese 10th Army lands at Jinshanwei on 5 November, and on 8 November the Chinese order a general retreat</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Wufu Line is penetrated on 19 November and the Xicheng Line given up on 26 November, and the fighting runs on to Nanjing</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/nanjing"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nanjing.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nanjing</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japanese forces take the city on 13 December and the Nanjing Massacre begins</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/shanghai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Shanghai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Shanghai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Battle of Shanghai ends in Japanese occupation of the Chinese-held districts</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/addis-ababa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Addis%20Ababa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Addis Ababa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Italian forces kill Ethiopians in Addis Ababa for three days after an attempt on Graziani's life</span></li></ul></section>
